  "reason": "The existing original Amiga rotation stores amiga_display_buffer_bases to app+4 and amiga_draw_buffer_bases to app+0 with index0/4/8 wrappingat12. The alternate-profile rotation uses the same roles with its own three-entry tables; alternate execution is not newly observed. Setup stores77B50 to both, so these are phase-dependent draw/display pointer roles, not exclusive front/back owners. View-row filling reads+0, and original/alternate text cursor/glyph paths read+4. CIA keyboard code atC91C readsSDR, inverts/rotatesD0, then testsbit7: press storesBYTE+138 and release storesBYTE+13A unchanged. Release retainsbit7. These are last decoded code bytes, not key-state booleans; no dead-storage or unobserved-path claim.",
